From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:21:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/45] firmware: qcom: scm: do not truncate the listener id

It arrives as a u64 from the secure world and selects which registered listener
services a request, so narrowing it silently is the wrong shape even though no
id today comes near the boundary.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
q706f-notes:
  Origin: https://github.com/wrobelda/linux branch qcom-qseecom-tee (v7.1 based),
          upstream commit 8405dec9eca075606bc591a4a93f111ae2b64bdf
          (exported in out/desktop/fp-eval/patches/qcom-qseecom-tee.patch, 11/45)
  Licence: GPL-2.0-only -- GPL-2.0 compatible
  Rebase onto 7.3.4: clean (git am, no fuzz)
  Our changes: none to the code; this note only

 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index f8122d5c7..7e1496556 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2205,7 +2205,10 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_service_listeners(struct qcom_scm_qseecom_resp *res)
 			return -ELOOP;
 		}
 
-		id = res->data;
+		if (res->data > U32_MAX)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	id = res->data;
 		listener = qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_find(id);
 		if (listener) {
 			status = listener->service(listener);
